<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 4th Grade (CEFR: A1.2)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> A Walk in the Neighborhood</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> This Is My Favorite.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b><br>
            Writing: productive: Write simple sentences on familiar topics.<br>
            interactive: Edit classmates' written work.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b><br>
            Writing: Can write simple sentences about favorite places (e.g., 'The park is fun.').<br>
            Can edit classmates' sentences about familiar places for clarity (e.g., change 'fun park' to 'The park is fun.').<br>
            Can revise sentences to add reasons using 'because' (e.g., 'I like the park because it has swings.').</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 34%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher greets students and displays pictures of different neighborhood places (park, street, playground, building, tree with flowers). The teacher asks students to quickly point and say the names of places they like. "What is your favorite place?" Students respond orally in short sentences like "The park!" or "I like the street." The teacher encourages them to use adjectives like "fun" or "beautiful" from previous lessons. The teacher transitions by saying, "Today, we will write about our favorite places!"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes on the board: "My favorite place is the park. It is the best because it has big swings." The teacher models the pronunciation of /b/ in 'best' and /f/ in 'favorite', and demonstrates blending onset /b/ and rhyme /ɪg/ to form 'big'. The teacher highlights 'best' (superlative) and 'because' (conjunction for reasons). The teacher explains that we write 'because' to tell *why* we like something.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is 'favorite' a place you don't like or a place you like very much?" (Expected answer: "Like very much.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say 'because,' am I telling *what* I like or *why* I like it?" (Expected answer: "Why I like it.")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short written "My Favorite Place" entry, possibly displayed on a projector or as a handout. It describes a child's favorite neighborhood spot. </p>
                <div style="background-color: #e6f2f8; padding: 10px; border-left: 3px solid #1a5276; margin-bottom: 10px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0;"><b>Example Text:</b><br>
                    Hi! My name is Ana. I want to tell you about my favorite place. My favorite place in the neighborhood is the big park. It is the best park because it has a huge playground. I like to run and play there. The park is beautiful, and I can see many colorful flowers. I visit the park often. It is a very fun place!</p>
                </div>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Written Expression: productive: Writes simple sentences on familiar topics, expressing opinions and preferences.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (Reading to understand writing structure):</b> The teacher reads the text aloud once, then students read silently. The teacher asks students to identify key information *that they will later use in their own writing*:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is Ana's favorite place?" (Gist question: "The big park.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Why does Ana like the park?" (Focus on 'because': "Because it has a huge playground.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Does Ana use words like 'best' or 'fun' to describe the park?" (True/False: "Yes, 'best' and 'fun'.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher highlights the structure of sentences where opinions are expressed and reasons are given.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Writing)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Writing simple sentences using superlatives ('the best'), simple present + conjunction ('because'), and neighborhood vocabulary (park, playground, street, building, flowers, fun, beautiful, big).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice - Sentence Completion:</b> The teacher provides a worksheet with incomplete sentences. Students complete them using vocabulary words from a word bank (e.g., 'park', 'playground', 'fun', 'beautiful', 'best', 'because').
                        <br>Example: "My favorite place is the _____. It is the _____ because it has a big _____."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice - Sentence Expansion:</b> The teacher gives simple statements. Students rewrite and expand them by adding 'because' and a reason, or using a superlative.
                        <br>Example: "I like the street." → "I like the street because it has tall trees." or "The street is the busiest street."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Guided Writing - Peer Check:</b> Students write two to three simple sentences about *their own* favorite neighborhood place, using at least one 'because' sentence and one superlative. For example: "My favorite place is the park. It is the best. I like the park because it has swings." After writing, they exchange their sentences with a partner. Partners check if the sentences make sense and if they used 'because'. This prepares them for interactive editing.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Individual written product (a short descriptive paragraph).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Description:</b> Students will write a short paragraph (3-5 sentences) titled "My Favorite Place in the Neighborhood." They must describe their favorite place, use 'because' to explain why they like it, and include at least one superlative (e.g., 'the best', 'the busiest', 'the coolest'). They should use vocabulary related to the neighborhood (e.g., park, street, playground, building, tree, flower, fun, beautiful, exciting).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Action:</b> The teacher circulates, offering support, checking for understanding, and encouraging students to use the target grammar and vocabulary. The teacher reminds students to write clear sentences.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Peer editing and revision using a simple checklist.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students exchange their "My Favorite Place" paragraphs from Stage 4 with a partner. Each student uses a simple checklist to review their partner's writing.
                <br><b>Peer Editing Checklist:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: square; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 4px; margin-bottom: 4px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did my partner name a favorite place? (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did my partner use "because" to explain why? (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did my partner use a superlative (e.g., 'best')? (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Are the sentences easy to understand? (Yes/No - if No, partner points to unclear sentence)</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students then return the edited papers and revise their own work based on the feedback. The teacher collects the revised paragraphs.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of sentences and ideas.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of target vocabulary (e.g., park, playground, fun, beautiful).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of 'because' to give reasons.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Attempted use of a superlative (e.g., 'the best').</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer on a small slip of paper:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did I write clear sentences about my favorite place?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did I use 'because' to explain why I like my favorite place?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was easy about writing about your favorite place today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was difficult or what do you want to practice more?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in helping students write about their favorite places and use 'because' and superlatives?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for students who struggled with sentence structure or applying 'because' in their writing? How effective was the peer editing process?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In the next lesson (Lesson 5: Mediation & Integration), students will use their written descriptions and the vocabulary learned to create a visual presentation or short 'tour guide' speech about their favorite neighborhood place, integrating their writing with visual aids and speaking to consolidate their learning.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>